From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:28:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8996-xiaomi-gemini: add CPU voltage
 scaling

The CPU OPP tables have no voltages and the CPUs have no supply, so
cpufreq changes the clock while VDD_APCC stays wherever the bootloader
left it. Raising the clock above what that voltage allows hangs the
phone.

Mainline has no CPR3 driver for MSM8996. Use the open-loop ceilings
of the downstream kernel instead (msm8996-regulator.dtsi,
qcom,cpr-voltage-ceiling, with the corner maps of msm8996-v3.dtsi),
which every chip must run at:

  power cluster   <= 1228.8 MHz  905 mV, above 1140 mV
  perf cluster    <= 1248.0 MHz  905 mV, above 1140 mV

The CBF frequency each OPP votes for stays inside the same corner.
The lower corners (670/745 mV) are left out on purpose: below 850 mV
the memory arrays have to be switched to the MX rail (APM) and below
700 mV the MEM-ACC settings have to change, and mainline drives
neither. Both clusters share the rail, so every OPP accepts up to
1140 mV and the regulator core picks the higher request.
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-xiaomi-gemini.dts   | 211 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 211 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-xiaomi-gemini.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-xiaomi-gemini.dts
index 9e9221746..3a2e2845a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-xiaomi-gemini.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-xiaomi-gemini.dts
@@ -116,6 +116,217 @@ synaptics@20 {
 
 };
 
+/*
+ * CPU voltage scaling. Mainline has no CPR3 driver for MSM8996, so use the
+ * downstream open-loop ceilings (msm8996-regulator.dtsi, qcom,cpr-voltage-ceiling),
+ * which are safe for every chip: 905 mV up to the NOM fuse corner
+ * (power cluster 1228.8 MHz, performance cluster 1248 MHz), 1140 mV above.
+ * The lower corners (670/745 mV) are not used: below 850 mV the memory arrays
+ * must move to the MX rail (APM) and below 700 mV the MEM-ACC settings must
+ * change, and mainline has drivers for neither.
+ * Both clusters share VDD_APCC, so each OPP allows up to 1140 mV and the
+ * regulator core settles on the higher of the two clusters' requests.
+ */
